316	### Why this is correct under concurrency
317	- **Single source of truth per invariant:** stock lives in a product aggregate,
318	  balance in a customer aggregate; their command streams serialize per aggregate
319	  (sequence-number optimistic concurrency), so no oversell / overdraw. Losing
320	  commands get `ConcurrencyException` and are retried.
321	- **Idempotency:** the order id is the aggregate id; a duplicate create command
322	  cannot create a second aggregate at sequence 0, and the confirm/reject method
323	  handlers are no-ops once status leaves PENDING.
324	- **Saga compensation:** charge failure triggers `ReleaseStockCommand` +
325	  `RejectOrderCommand`.
326	- **Exactly-once notification:** the projection writes the read-model row and the
327	  notification in the processor's transaction (token advances with it); the
328	  `UNIQUE(orderId)` makes a replayed event idempotent (at-least-once → effectively
329	  once).
330	- **Eventual consistency:** views update when the tracking processor polls;
331	  `GET` may briefly 404 until the projection catches up — clients poll within the
332	  convergence window.
